      },
      "message": "feat(post): Cobra Cut D 0.25 qualities for one 40 mm Agie punch\n\nTwo new machine conditions select two new work qualities:\nAGIE_COBRA_RA030 requests CCD030 (Ra 0.30, main cut and three trims)\nand AGIE_COBRA_RA070 requests CCD070 (Ra 0.70, main cut and two trims).\n\n- agie_setup::Quality gets Ccd030 and Ccd070 with the measured 40 mm\n  offsets 250/170/145/135 and 245/165/140 um, and a wire() name.\n- The piece and each work set ID_THREAD from the quality. The Berco\n  qualities keep every golden byte.\n- The clearance and miter checks use the rough offset of the quality.\n- The encoder refuses other heights (UnqualifiedCobraHeight). The post\n  refuses a die, an open cutoff, a group and a DXF arc punch, and names\n  the selected condition.\n\nFixes #2986\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
